CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ terminate called from the unwinding: SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed (soundness): the exception lowering assumed that a destructor
called during stack unwinding does not exit via an exception, so the path
on which std::terminate calls the handler was removed.  It now calls
std::terminate there; std::set_terminate and std::terminate have models.
